-- coa22-part31-ch1.l4: Part 31, Chapter 1 (Striking off) of the Companies Act 2006 (United Kingdom), ss 1000 to 1011
-- (lines 13994-14197 of ukpga-2006-46.txt). LAYER 1: the law, objectively.
--
-- SOURCE. A plain-text rendering of the Act from legislation.gov.uk made by a converter script; it is not the
-- official text and nothing here is "verified against the official text". Quote lines are copied from it by a
-- script and checked by srcrefs.py.
--
-- HOW TO READ AN ANSWER (the rule of 2026-10-29, assumed, not ruled by a lawyer; see NOTES.md).
--   JUST TRUE   the text says the case is within the rule.
--   JUST FALSE  the text says no in its own words (a "means" definition, an "if" / "where" / "unless" / "until" /
--               "within" condition that fails, a flat negative). Each such branch carries
--               -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "<words>"
--   NOTHING     the text does not decide (silent, list not closed, includes, undefined term, points outside the
--               text, limited by its own wording). Each such branch carries  -- NOTHING-kind (<why>)
--   A caller must never turn NOTHING into FALSE.
-- Facts a witness can state, and judgments the text hands to someone else (the registrar has reasonable cause to
-- believe), are BOOLEAN inputs. Answers other parts give are MAYBE BOOLEAN inputs named for the section that answers.
-- Days are counted by adding them to the date of the event (the day of the event is not counted); months by
-- `add months` (the corresponding day of the later month, the last day of a shorter month). NOTES.md, fork F1.
-- The text counts "the expiration of 2 months from the date of the notice" as ending on the date that is two months
-- after the notice; the registrar may act on a later day. NOTES.md, fork F4.

§ `Part 31 -- Dissolution and restoration to the register`

§§ `Chapter 1 -- Striking off`

§§§ `Registrar's power to strike off defunct company`

-- ---- s 1000: Power to strike off company not carrying on business or in operation -------------------------

-- (1) If the registrar has reasonable cause to believe that a company is not carrying on business or in operation,
-- the registrar may send the company a communication inquiring whether it is.
-- src:13998 | (1) If the registrar has reasonable cause to believe that a company is not carrying on business or in operation, the registrar may send to the company a communication inquiring whether the company is carrying on business or in operation.
@ref s 1000(1) Power to strike off company not carrying on business or in operation (src:13998)
GIVEN `the registrar has reasonable cause to believe that the company is not carrying on business or in operation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1000(1) the registrar may send the company a communication inquiring whether it is carrying on business or in operation` MEANS
    IF `the registrar has reasonable cause to believe that the company is not carrying on business or in operation`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If the registrar has reasonable cause to believe that a company is not carrying on business or in operation, the registrar may send"; the registrar has no such cause, and the text does not say that he may not (name-test sweep of 2026-11-12, fork F19: the other reading is JUST FALSE, a failed "if" read as the text's own no)

-- (2) If the registrar does not within 14 days of sending the communication receive any answer to it, the registrar
-- must within 14 days after the expiration of that period send a second communication.
-- src:13999 | (2) If the registrar does not within 14 days of sending the communication receive any answer to it, the registrar must within 14 days after the expiration of that period send to the company a second communication referring to the first communication, and stating—
-- src:14000 | (a) that no answer to it has been received, and
-- src:14001 | (b) that if an answer is not received to the second communication within 14 days from its date, a notice will be published in the Gazette with a view to striking the company's name off the register.
@ref s 1000(2) Power to strike off company not carrying on business or in operation (src:13999-14001)
GIVEN `the date the first communication was sent` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 1000(2) the last day of the 14 days for an answer to the first communication` MEANS
    `the date the first communication was sent` PLUS 14

@ref s 1000(2) Power to strike off company not carrying on business or in operation (src:13999-14001)
GIVEN `the date the first communication was sent` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 1000(2) the last day for the registrar to send the second communication` MEANS
    `s 1000(2) the last day of the 14 days for an answer to the first communication` `the date the first communication was sent` PLUS 14

@ref s 1000(2) Power to strike off company not carrying on business or in operation (src:13999-14001)
GIVEN `the date the first communication was sent` IS A DATE
      `the date an answer to the first communication was received, if one was` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the date asked about` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1000(2) the registrar must send a second communication` MEANS
    IF `the date asked about` AT MOST `s 1000(2) the last day of the 14 days for an answer to the first communication` `the date the first communication was sent`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If the registrar does not within 14 days of sending the communication receive any answer to it" (the 14 days have not yet expired)
    ELSE CONSIDER `the date an answer to the first communication was received, if one was`
         WHEN NOTHING THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN JUST answered THEN
             IF answered AT MOST `s 1000(2) the last day of the 14 days for an answer to the first communication` `the date the first communication was sent`
             THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If the registrar does not within 14 days of sending the communication receive any answer to it" (an answer came in time)
             ELSE JUST TRUE

@ref s 1000(2) Power to strike off company not carrying on business or in operation (src:13999-14001)
GIVEN `the date the first communication was sent` IS A DATE
      `the date the second communication was sent` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1000(2) the second communication was sent within the time allowed` MEANS
