-- ---- s 1001: Duty to act in case of company being wound up -------------------------------------------------

-- (1) If, in a case where a company is being wound up, (a) the registrar has reasonable cause to believe (i) that no
-- liquidator is acting, or (ii) that the affairs of the company are fully wound up, and (b) the returns required to
-- be made by the liquidator have not been made for six consecutive months, the registrar must publish in the Gazette
-- and send to the company or the liquidator (if any) a notice of intended striking off, after 2 months.
-- src:14013 | (1) If, in a case where a company is being wound up—
-- src:14014 | (a) the registrar has reasonable cause to believe—
-- src:14015 | (i) that no liquidator is acting, or
-- src:14016 | (ii) that the affairs of the company are fully wound up, and
-- src:14017 | (b) the returns required to be made by the liquidator have not been made for a period of six consecutive months,
-- src:14018 | the registrar must publish in the Gazette and send to the company or the liquidator (if any) a notice that at the expiration of 2 months from the date of the notice the name of the company mentioned in it will, unless cause is shown to the contrary, be struck off the register and the company will be dissolved.
@ref s 1001(1) Duty to act in case of company being wound up (src:14013-14018)
GIVEN `the company is being wound up` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the registrar has reasonable cause to believe that no liquidator is acting` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the registrar has reasonable cause to believe that the affairs of the company are fully wound up` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the returns required to be made by the liquidator have not been made for a period of six consecutive months` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1001(1) the registrar must publish in the Gazette and send the notice of intended striking off` MEANS
    IF     `the company is being wound up`
       AND (   `the registrar has reasonable cause to believe that no liquidator is acting`
            OR `the registrar has reasonable cause to believe that the affairs of the company are fully wound up`)
       AND `the returns required to be made by the liquidator have not been made for a period of six consecutive months`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If, in a case where a company is being wound up— (a) the registrar has reasonable cause to believe— (i) that no liquidator is acting, or (ii) that the affairs of the company are fully wound up, and (b) the returns required to be made by the liquidator have not been made for a period of six consecutive months"

