-- ---- s 1002: Supplementary provisions as to service of communication or notice ------------------------------

-- (1) If the registrar is not able to send a communication or notice under section 1000 or 1001 to a company in
-- accordance with Schedule 4, the communication may be sent to an officer of the company at an address for that
-- officer that has been notified to the registrar by the company. Schedule 4 is coa29's (a seam).
-- src:14026 | (1) If the registrar is not able to send a communication or notice under section 1000 or 1001 to a company in accordance with Schedule 4, the communication may be sent to an officer of the company at an address for that officer that has been notified to the registrar by the company.
@ref s 1002(1) Supplementary provisions as to service of communication or notice (src:14026)
GIVEN `sch 4 the registrar is able to send the communication or notice to the company in accordance with Schedule 4` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the officer has an address that has been notified to the registrar by the company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1002(1) the communication may be sent to an officer of the company at the address notified` MEANS
    CONSIDER `sch 4 the registrar is able to send the communication or notice to the company in accordance with Schedule 4`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the registrar is able to send it in accordance with Schedule 4 is Schedule 4's answer
    WHEN JUST able THEN
        IF able
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If the registrar is not able to send a communication or notice under section 1000 or 1001 to a company in accordance with Schedule 4" (the registrar is able, and the text does not say that the communication may not then be sent to an officer) (name-test sweep of 2026-11-12, fork F21: the other reading is JUST FALSE, a failed "if" read as the text's own no)
        ELSE IF `the officer has an address that has been notified to the registrar by the company`
             THEN JUST TRUE
             ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "an officer of the company at an address for that officer that has been notified to the registrar by the company"; no address is notified, so the grant, which is limited to that address, says nothing (the same fork F21: the other reading is JUST FALSE)

