-- (3) A notice to be sent to a liquidator under section 1001 may be sent to the address of the liquidator's last
-- known place of business or to an address specified by the liquidator to the registrar for receiving notices.
-- src:14028 | (3) A notice to be sent to a liquidator under section 1001 may be sent to the address of the liquidator’s last known place of business or to an address specified by the liquidator to the registrar for the purpose of receiving notices, or notices of that kind.
@ref s 1002(3) Supplementary provisions as to service of communication or notice (src:14028)
GIVEN `the notice is one to be sent to a liquidator under section 1001` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is sent to the address of the liquidator's last known place of business` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is sent to an address specified by the liquidator to the registrar for the purpose of receiving notices, or notices of that kind` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1002(3) the notice to the liquidator may be sent to the address` MEANS
    IF `the notice is one to be sent to a liquidator under section 1001`
    THEN IF     `it is sent to the address of the liquidator's last known place of business`
            OR  `it is sent to an address specified by the liquidator to the registrar for the purpose of receiving notices, or notices of that kind`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "may be sent to the address of the liquidator’s last known place of business or to an address specified"; a grant, and no "only" closes it
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A notice to be sent to a liquidator under section 1001"

-- (4) In section 1002 "address" has the same meaning as in section 1148(1): it includes a number or address used for
-- sending or receiving documents or information by electronic means.
-- src:14029 | (4) In this section “address” has the same meaning as in section 1148(1).
@ref s 1002(4) Supplementary provisions as to service of communication or notice (src:14029)
GIVEN `it is a number or address used for the purposes of sending or receiving documents or information by electronic means` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1002(4) the number or address is an address for the purposes of section 1002` MEANS
    IF `it is a number or address used for the purposes of sending or receiving documents or information by electronic means`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "“address” includes a number or address used for the purposes of sending or receiving documents or information by electronic means" (section 1148(1)), which does not close the term

§§§ `Registrar's power to strike off company registered on false basis`

-- ---- s 1002A: Power to strike off company registered on false basis -----------------------------------------

-- (1) The registrar may strike a company's name off the register if the registrar has reasonable cause to believe
-- that (a) information in the application for registration (or for restoration) is misleading, false or deceptive in
-- a material particular, or (b) any statement made to the registrar in connection with such an application is.
-- src:14032 | (1) The registrar may strike a company’s name off the register if the registrar has reasonable cause to believe that—
-- src:14033 | (a) any information contained in the application for the registration of the company, or in any application for restoration of the company to the register, is misleading, false or deceptive in a material particular, or
-- src:14034 | (b) any statement made to the registrar in connection with such an application is misleading, false or deceptive in a material particular.
@ref s 1002A(1) Power to strike off company registered on false basis (src:14032-14034)
GIVEN `the registrar has reasonable cause to believe that information contained in the application for the registration of the company, or in any application for restoration of the company to the register, is misleading, false or deceptive in a material particular` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the registrar has reasonable cause to believe that a statement made to the registrar in connection with such an application is misleading, false or deceptive in a material particular` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 1002A(3) the registrar may not yet exercise the power in subsection (1)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1002A(1) the registrar may strike the company's name off the register` MEANS
    IF `s 1002A(3) the registrar may not yet exercise the power in subsection (1)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The registrar may not exercise the power in subsection (1) unless"
    ELSE IF `s 1002A(3) the registrar may not yet exercise the power in subsection (1)` EQUALS NOTHING
         THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the notice period has run is not known
         ELSE IF     `the registrar has reasonable cause to believe that information contained in the application for the registration of the company, or in any application for restoration of the company to the register, is misleading, false or deceptive in a material particular`
                 OR  `the registrar has reasonable cause to believe that a statement made to the registrar in connection with such an application is misleading, false or deceptive in a material particular`
              THEN JUST TRUE
              ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "if the registrar has reasonable cause to believe that"; the registrar has no such cause, and the text does not say that he may not strike off (the bar "may not exercise the power ... unless" above stays JUST FALSE) (name-test sweep of 2026-11-12, fork F23: the other reading is JUST FALSE, a failed "if" read as the text's own no)

-- (2) In subsection (1) the reference to an application includes any documents delivered to the registrar in
-- connection with the application.
-- src:14035 | (2) In subsection (1) the reference to an application includes any documents delivered to the registrar in connection with the application.
@ref s 1002A(2) Power to strike off company registered on false basis (src:14035)
GIVEN `the document was delivered to the registrar in connection with the application` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1002A(2) the document is part of the application for the purposes of subsection (1)` MEANS
    IF `the document was delivered to the registrar in connection with the application`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "the reference to an application includes any documents delivered to the registrar in connection with the application"

-- (3) The registrar may not exercise the power in subsection (1) unless (a) the registrar has published a notice in
-- the Gazette that, at the end of the period of 28 days beginning with the date of the notice, the name will, unless
-- cause is shown to the contrary, be struck off and the company dissolved, and (b) that period has expired.
-- The 28 days begin with the date of the notice, so the last day of the period is 27 days after it.
-- src:14036 | (3) The registrar may not exercise the power in subsection (1) unless—
-- src:14037 | (a) the registrar has published a notice in the Gazette that, at the end of the period of 28 days beginning with the date of the notice, the name of the company mentioned in the notice will, unless cause is shown to the contrary, be struck off the register and the company will be dissolved, and
-- src:14038 | (b) the period mentioned in paragraph (a) has expired.
@ref s 1002A(3) Power to strike off company registered on false basis (src:14036-14038)
GIVEN `the date of the notice published in the Gazette` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 1002A(3) the last day of the period of 28 days beginning with the date of the notice` MEANS
    `the date of the notice published in the Gazette` PLUS 27

@ref s 1002A(3) Power to strike off company registered on false basis (src:14036-14038)
GIVEN `the registrar has published a notice in the Gazette of the kind described in paragraph (a)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date of the notice published in the Gazette` IS A DATE
      `the date asked about` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1002A(3) the registrar may not yet exercise the power in subsection (1)` MEANS
    IF     `the registrar has published a notice in the Gazette of the kind described in paragraph (a)`
       AND `the date asked about` GREATER THAN `s 1002A(3) the last day of the period of 28 days beginning with the date of the notice` `the date of the notice published in the Gazette`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The registrar may not exercise the power in subsection (1) unless" (the notice is published and its period has expired, so the bar no longer applies)
    ELSE JUST TRUE

-- (4) If the registrar exercises the power in subsection (1), the registrar must publish a notice in the Gazette.
-- src:14039 | (4) If the registrar exercises the power in subsection (1), the registrar must publish a notice in the Gazette of the company’s name having been struck off the register.
@ref s 1002A(4) Power to strike off company registered on false basis (src:14039)
GIVEN `the registrar has struck the company's name off the register` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1002A(4) the registrar must publish notice in the Gazette of the company's name having been struck off` MEANS
    IF `the registrar has struck the company's name off the register`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If the registrar exercises the power in subsection (1), the registrar must publish a notice in the Gazette of the company’s name having been struck off the register" (the "If" is not met)


-- (5) On the publication of the notice in the Gazette the company is dissolved.
-- src:14040 | (5) On the publication of the notice in the Gazette the company is dissolved.
@ref s 1002A(5) Power to strike off company registered on false basis (src:14040)
GIVEN `the date the notice of the striking off was published in the Gazette, if it has been` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the date asked about` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1002A(5) the company is dissolved` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the date the notice of the striking off was published in the Gazette, if it has been`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "On the publication of the notice in the Gazette the company is dissolved" (no publication has happened)
    WHEN JUST published THEN
        IF published AT MOST `the date asked about`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "On the publication of the notice in the Gazette the company is dissolved" (the publication is later than the date asked about)


-- (6) However (a) the liability (if any) of every director, managing officer or member continues ..., and (b) ...
-- src:14041 | (6) However—
-- src:14042 | (a) the liability (if any) of every director, managing officer or member of the company continues and may be enforced as if the company had not been dissolved, and
-- src:14043 | (b) nothing in this section affects the power of the court to wind up a company the name of which has been struck off the register.
@ref s 1002A(6) Power to strike off company registered on false basis (src:14041-14043)
GIVEN `s 1002A(6) the company is dissolved` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person is a director, managing officer or member of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has a liability` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1002A(6)(a) the liability of the person continues and may be enforced as if the company had not been dissolved` MEANS
    IF     `s 1002A(6) the company is dissolved` EQUALS JUST TRUE
       AND `the person is a director, managing officer or member of the company`
       AND `the person has a liability`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the liability (if any) of every director, managing officer or member of the company continues"; where the company is not dissolved, or the person is not named, or has no liability, nothing is said

@ref s 1002A(6) Power to strike off company registered on false basis (src:14041-14043)
GIVEN `the company's name has been struck off the register under this section` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1002A(6)(b) nothing in the section affects the power of the court to wind up the company` MEANS
    IF `the company's name has been struck off the register under this section`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a company the name of which has been struck off the register"; no statement about any other company


§§§ `Voluntary striking off`

-- ---- s 1003: Striking off on application by company ----------------------------------------------------------

-- (1) On application by a company, the registrar of companies may strike the company's name off the register.
-- src:14046 | (1) On application by a company, the registrar of companies may strike the company's name off the register.
@ref s 1003(1) Striking off on application by company (src:14046)
GIVEN `the company has applied to the registrar to be struck off the register` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1003(1) the registrar may strike the company's name off the register on application by the company` MEANS
    IF `the company has applied to the registrar to be struck off the register`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "On application by a company, the registrar of companies may strike the company's name off the register" (no application has been made)

-- (2)(a) The application must be made on the company's behalf by its directors or by a majority of them.
-- src:14047 | (2) The application—
-- src:14048 | (a) must be made on the company's behalf by its directors or by a majority of them, and
@ref s 1003(2)(a) Striking off on application by company (src:14047-14048)
GIVEN `the number of directors who make the application on the company's behalf` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of directors of the company` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1003(2)(a) the application is made on the company's behalf by its directors or by a majority of them` MEANS
    IF     `the number of directors of the company` GREATER THAN 0
       AND `the number of directors who make the application on the company's behalf` TIMES 2 GREATER THAN `the number of directors of the company`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must be made on the company's behalf by its directors or by a majority of them" (a bare "must" not done: fork F6; "a majority" is read as more than half)

-- (2)(b) The application must contain the prescribed information (what is prescribed is outside the sources).
-- src:14047 | (2) The application—
-- src:14048 | (a) must be made on the company's behalf by its directors or by a majority of them, and
-- src:14049 | (b) must contain the prescribed information.
@ref s 1003(2)(b) Striking off on application by company (src:14047-14049)
GIVEN `the application contains the prescribed information` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1003(2)(b) the application contains the prescribed information` MEANS
    IF `the application contains the prescribed information`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must contain the prescribed information" (a bare "must" not done: fork F6)

-- (3) The registrar may not strike a company off under this section until after the expiration of 2 months from the
-- publication in the Gazette of a notice (a) stating that the registrar may exercise the power, and (b) inviting any
-- person to show cause why that should not be done. Encoded as the bar, as ruled 2026-11-05 (d): JUST TRUE while the
-- registrar is barred, JUST FALSE once the 2 months have expired after a notice of that kind.
-- src:14050 | (3) The registrar may not strike a company off under this section until after the expiration of 2 months from the publication by the registrar in the Gazette of a notice—
-- src:14051 | (a) stating that the registrar may exercise the power under this section in relation to the company, and
-- src:14052 | (b) inviting any person to show cause why that should not be done.
@ref s 1003(3) Striking off on application by company (src:14050-14052)
GIVEN `the date the notice was published in the Gazette, if it has been` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the notice states that the registrar may exercise the power under section 1003 in relation to the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice invites any person to show cause why that should not be done` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date asked about` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1003(3) the registrar is barred from striking the company off under section 1003` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the date the notice was published in the Gazette, if it has been`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN JUST published THEN
        IF     `the notice states that the registrar may exercise the power under section 1003 in relation to the company`
           AND `the notice invites any person to show cause why that should not be done`
           AND `the date asked about` GREATER THAN `add months` published 2
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "may not strike a company off under this section until after the expiration of 2 months from the publication" (the 2 months have expired after a notice of the required kind)
        ELSE JUST TRUE

-- (4) The registrar must publish notice in the Gazette of the company's name having been struck off.
-- src:14053 | (4) The registrar must publish notice in the Gazette of the company's name having been struck off.
@ref s 1003(4) Striking off on application by company (src:14053)
GIVEN `the registrar has struck the company's name off the register` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1003(4) the registrar must publish notice in the Gazette of the company's name having been struck off` MEANS
    IF `the registrar has struck the company's name off the register`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): "The registrar must publish notice in the Gazette of the company's name having been struck off"; a bare "must" with no stated occasion, and no striking off has happened (fork F5)


-- (5) On the publication of the notice in the Gazette the company is dissolved.
-- src:14054 | (5) On the publication of the notice in the Gazette the company is dissolved.
@ref s 1003(5) Striking off on application by company (src:14054)
GIVEN `the date the notice of the striking off was published in the Gazette, if it has been` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the date asked about` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1003(5) the company is dissolved` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the date the notice of the striking off was published in the Gazette, if it has been`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "On the publication of the notice in the Gazette the company is dissolved" (no publication has happened)
    WHEN JUST published THEN
        IF published AT MOST `the date asked about`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "On the publication of the notice in the Gazette the company is dissolved" (the publication is later than the date asked about)


-- (6) However (a) the liability (if any) of every director, managing officer and member continues ..., and (b) ...
-- src:14055 | (6) However—
-- src:14056 | (a) the liability (if any) of every director, managing officer and member of the company continues and may be enforced as if the company had not been dissolved, and
-- src:14057 | (b) nothing in this section affects the power of the court to wind up a company the name of which has been struck off the register.
@ref s 1003(6) Striking off on application by company (src:14055-14057)
GIVEN `s 1003(6) the company is dissolved` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person is a director, managing officer or member of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has a liability` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1003(6)(a) the liability of the person continues and may be enforced as if the company had not been dissolved` MEANS
    IF     `s 1003(6) the company is dissolved` EQUALS JUST TRUE
       AND `the person is a director, managing officer or member of the company`
       AND `the person has a liability`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the liability (if any) of every director, managing officer and member of the company continues"; where the company is not dissolved, or the person is not named, or has no liability, nothing is said

@ref s 1003(6) Striking off on application by company (src:14055-14057)
GIVEN `the company's name has been struck off the register under this section` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1003(6)(b) nothing in the section affects the power of the court to wind up the company` MEANS
    IF `the company's name has been struck off the register under this section`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a company the name of which has been struck off the register"; no statement about any other company


-- ---- s 1004: Circumstances in which application not to be made: activities of company -----------------------

-- (1) An application under section 1003 on behalf of a company must not be made if, at any time in the previous
-- three months, the company has (a) changed its name, (b) traded or otherwise carried on business, (c) made a
-- disposal for value of property or rights it held for disposal for gain, or (d) engaged in any other activity,
-- except one that is necessary or expedient for an application, concluding the company's affairs, complying with a
-- statutory requirement, or specified by the Secretary of State by order. The three months are the Act's figure; the
-- Secretary of State may alter them by order (subsection (3), inert), and a substitution would change these answers.
-- src:14059 | (1) An application under section 1003 (application for voluntary striking off) on behalf of a company must not be made if, at any time in the previous three months, the company has—
-- src:14060 | (a) changed its name,
-- src:14061 | (b) traded or otherwise carried on business,
-- src:14062 | (c) made a disposal for value of property or rights that, immediately before ceasing to trade or otherwise carry on business, it held for the purpose of disposal for gain in the normal course of trading or otherwise carrying on business, or
-- src:14063 | (d) engaged in any other activity, except one which is—
-- src:14064 | (i) necessary or expedient for the purpose of making an application under that section, or deciding whether to do so,
-- src:14065 | (ii) necessary or expedient for the purpose of concluding the affairs of the company,
-- src:14066 | (iii) necessary or expedient for the purpose of complying with any statutory requirement, or
-- src:14067 | (iv) specified by the Secretary of State by order for the purposes of this sub-paragraph.
@ref s 1004(1) Circumstances in which application not to be made: activities of company (src:14059-14067)
GIVEN `the date of the activity` IS A DATE
      `the date of the application` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1004(1) the date falls within the three months before the date of the application` MEANS
    IF     `the date of the activity` AT MOST `the date of the application`
       AND `add months` `the date of the activity` 3 AT LEAST `the date of the application`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "at any time in the previous three months" (the date is outside that period; the period is read as the three months ending with the date of the application: fork F7)

-- (2) For the purposes of section 1004 a company is not to be treated as trading or otherwise carrying on business
-- by virtue only of the fact that it makes a payment in respect of a liability incurred in the course of trading.
-- src:14068 | (2) For the purposes of this section, a company is not to be treated as trading or otherwise carrying on business by virtue only of the fact that it makes a payment in respect of a liability incurred in the course of trading or otherwise carrying on business.
@ref s 1004(2) Circumstances in which application not to be made: activities of company (src:14068)
GIVEN `the company traded or otherwise carried on business` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the only reason is that the company makes a payment in respect of a liability incurred in the course of trading or otherwise carrying on business` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1004(2) the company is to be treated as trading or otherwise carrying on business` MEANS
    IF `the only reason is that the company makes a payment in respect of a liability incurred in the course of trading or otherwise carrying on business`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a company is not to be treated as trading or otherwise carrying on business by virtue only of the fact that it makes a payment in respect of a liability incurred in the course of trading or otherwise carrying on business"
    ELSE IF `the company traded or otherwise carried on business`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection says when a company is not treated as trading, and says nothing about a company that did not trade

-- (1)(d) Engaged in any other activity, except one which is (i) necessary or expedient for the purpose of making an
-- application under section 1003, or deciding whether to do so, (ii) for concluding the affairs of the company,
-- (iii) for complying with any statutory requirement, or (iv) specified by the Secretary of State by order.
-- src:14063 | (d) engaged in any other activity, except one which is—
-- src:14064 | (i) necessary or expedient for the purpose of making an application under that section, or deciding whether to do so,
-- src:14065 | (ii) necessary or expedient for the purpose of concluding the affairs of the company,
-- src:14066 | (iii) necessary or expedient for the purpose of complying with any statutory requirement, or
-- src:14067 | (iv) specified by the Secretary of State by order for the purposes of this sub-paragraph.
@ref s 1004(1)(d) Circumstances in which application not to be made: activities of company (src:14063-14067)
GIVEN `the company engaged in some other activity` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the activity was necessary or expedient for the purpose of making an application under section 1003, or deciding whether to do so` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the activity was necessary or expedient for the purpose of concluding the affairs of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the activity was necessary or expedient for the purpose of complying with any statutory requirement` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the activity is specified by the Secretary of State by order for the purposes of section 1004(1)(d)(iv)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1004(1)(d) the company engaged in an activity that is not an excepted one` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the company engaged in some other activity`)
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(d) engaged in any other activity" (the company engaged in no other activity)
    ELSE IF     `the activity was necessary or expedient for the purpose of making an application under section 1003, or deciding whether to do so`
            OR  `the activity was necessary or expedient for the purpose of concluding the affairs of the company`
            OR  `the activity was necessary or expedient for the purpose of complying with any statutory requirement`
            OR  `the activity is specified by the Secretary of State by order for the purposes of section 1004(1)(d)(iv)`
         THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "except one which is— (i) necessary or expedient"
         ELSE JUST TRUE

-- (1) The prohibition: the application must not be made if any of the four things happened in the period. The four
-- inputs are already limited to the period (see the function above): (a), (b) as treated by subsection (2), (c), (d).
-- src:14059 | (1) An application under section 1003 (application for voluntary striking off) on behalf of a company must not be made if, at any time in the previous three months, the company has—
-- src:14060 | (a) changed its name,
-- src:14061 | (b) traded or otherwise carried on business,
-- src:14062 | (c) made a disposal for value of property or rights that, immediately before ceasing to trade or otherwise carry on business, it held for the purpose of disposal for gain in the normal course of trading or otherwise carrying on business, or
-- src:14063 | (d) engaged in any other activity, except one which is—
-- src:14064 | (i) necessary or expedient for the purpose of making an application under that section, or deciding whether to do so,
-- src:14065 | (ii) necessary or expedient for the purpose of concluding the affairs of the company,
-- src:14066 | (iii) necessary or expedient for the purpose of complying with any statutory requirement, or
-- src:14067 | (iv) specified by the Secretary of State by order for the purposes of this sub-paragraph.
@ref s 1004(1) Circumstances in which application not to be made: activities of company (src:14059-14067)
GIVEN `at some time in the previous three months the company changed its name` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 1004(2) the company is to be treated as trading or otherwise carrying on business` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `at some time in the previous three months the company made a disposal for value of property or rights that, immediately before ceasing to trade or otherwise carry on business, it held for the purpose of disposal for gain in the normal course of trading or otherwise carrying on business` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 1004(1)(d) the company engaged in an activity that is not an excepted one` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1004(1) the application must not be made` MEANS
    IF     `at some time in the previous three months the company changed its name`
       OR  `s 1004(2) the company is to be treated as trading or otherwise carrying on business` EQUALS JUST TRUE
       OR  `at some time in the previous three months the company made a disposal for value of property or rights that, immediately before ceasing to trade or otherwise carry on business, it held for the purpose of disposal for gain in the normal course of trading or otherwise carrying on business`
       OR  `s 1004(1)(d) the company engaged in an activity that is not an excepted one` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must not be made if, at any time in the previous three months, the company has— (a) changed its name, (b) traded or otherwise carried on business, (c) made a disposal for value of property or rights"

-- (1) as a regulative rule: a director SHANT make the application (no time limit: the text gives none).
DECLARE `s 1004 act of the director` IS ONE OF
    `s 1004 make an application under section 1003 on behalf of the company`

-- src:14059 | (1) An application under section 1003 (application for voluntary striking off) on behalf of a company must not be made if, at any time in the previous three months, the company has—
-- src:14060 | (a) changed its name,
-- src:14061 | (b) traded or otherwise carried on business,
-- src:14062 | (c) made a disposal for value of property or rights that, immediately before ceasing to trade or otherwise carry on business, it held for the purpose of disposal for gain in the normal course of trading or otherwise carrying on business, or
-- src:14063 | (d) engaged in any other activity, except one which is—
-- src:14064 | (i) necessary or expedient for the purpose of making an application under that section, or deciding whether to do so,
-- src:14065 | (ii) necessary or expedient for the purpose of concluding the affairs of the company,
-- src:14066 | (iii) necessary or expedient for the purpose of complying with any statutory requirement, or
-- src:14067 | (iv) specified by the Secretary of State by order for the purposes of this sub-paragraph.
@ref s 1004(1) Circumstances in which application not to be made: activities of company (src:14059-14067)
GIVEN `s 1004(1) the application must not be made` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 1004 act of the director`
`s 1004(1) the director's duty not to make the application` MEANS
    IF `s 1004(1) the application must not be made` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN PARTY Director
         SHANT `s 1004 make an application under section 1003 on behalf of the company`
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST BREACH BY Director BECAUSE "an application under section 1003 was made when the company had in the previous three months changed its name, traded, made a disposal for value, or engaged in another activity"
    ELSE FULFILLED

-- (3) The Secretary of State may by order amend subsection (1) for the purpose of altering the period; (4) an order is
-- subject to negative resolution procedure. Inert, reason 2 (order-making power and its procedure).
-- src:14069 | (3) The Secretary of State may by order amend subsection (1) for the purpose of altering the period in relation to which the doing of the things mentioned in paragraphs (a) to (d) of that subsection is relevant.
-- src:14070 | (4) An order under this section is subject to negative resolution procedure.
§§§ `s 1004(3)-(4) Orders altering the period (inert: machinery)`

-- (5) It is an offence for a person to make an application in contravention of this section.
-- src:14071 | (5) It is an offence for a person to make an application in contravention of this section.
@ref s 1004(5) Circumstances in which application not to be made: activities of company (src:14071)
GIVEN `s 1004(1) the application must not be made` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person makes the application` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1004(5) the person commits an offence by making the application` MEANS
    IF `s 1004(1) the application must not be made` EQUALS JUST TRUE AND `the person makes the application`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "It is an offence for a person to make an application in contravention of this section"; an application not in contravention is not mentioned (marginal reading (b))


-- (6) In proceedings for such an offence it is a defence to prove that he did not know, and could not reasonably have
-- known, of the existence of the facts that led to the contravention.
