      `the accused proves that he could not reasonably have known of the existence of the facts that led to the contravention` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1004(6) section 1004 gives the accused a defence on these facts` MEANS
    IF     `the accused proves that he did not know of the existence of the facts that led to the contravention`
       AND `the accused proves that he could not reasonably have known of the existence of the facts that led to the contravention`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "it is a defence for the accused to prove that he did not know, and could not reasonably have known, of the existence of the facts that led to the contravention" (this section gives no defence on these facts, ruled 2026-11-05 (b))


