        (Penalty OF `on summary conviction`, NOTHING, JUST (`a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum` 1), NOTHING, FALSE)


-- ---- s 1005: Circumstances in which application not to be made: other proceedings not concluded -------------

-- (2) For the purposes of subsection (1)(a) the matter is finally concluded if (a) the application has been
-- withdrawn, (b) the application has been finally dealt with without a compromise or arrangement being sanctioned
-- by the court, or (c) a compromise or arrangement has been sanctioned and fully carried out.
-- src:14085 | (2) For the purposes of subsection (1)(a), the matter is finally concluded if—
-- src:14086 | (a) the application has been withdrawn,
-- src:14087 | (b) the application has been finally dealt with without a compromise or arrangement being sanctioned by the court, or
-- src:14088 | (c) a compromise or arrangement has been sanctioned by the court and has, together with anything required to be done under any provision made in relation to the matter by order of the court, been fully carried out.
@ref s 1005(2) Circumstances in which application not to be made: other proceedings not concluded (src:14085-14088)
GIVEN `the application to the court under Part 26 or 26A has been withdrawn` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the application has been finally dealt with without a compromise or arrangement being sanctioned by the court` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a compromise or arrangement has been sanctioned by the court and has, together with anything required to be done under any provision made in relation to the matter by order of the court, been fully carried out` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1005(2) the matter of the application to the court under Part 26 or 26A is finally concluded` MEANS
    IF     `the application to the court under Part 26 or 26A has been withdrawn`
       OR  `the application has been finally dealt with without a compromise or arrangement being sanctioned by the court`
       OR  `a compromise or arrangement has been sanctioned by the court and has, together with anything required to be done under any provision made in relation to the matter by order of the court, been fully carried out`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the matter is finally concluded if—"

-- (3) For the purposes of subsection (1)(b) the matter is finally concluded if (a) no meetings are to be summoned
-- under section 3 of the Insolvency Act 1986 or Article 16 of the 1989 Order, (b) meetings summoned fail to approve
-- the arrangement with no, or the same, modifications, (c) an approved arrangement has been fully implemented, or
-- (d) the court revokes approval under section 6(5) or Article 19(5) and the company has done whatever it is required
-- to do under any directions given under section 6(6) or Article 19(6).
-- src:14089 | (3) For the purposes of subsection (1)(b), the matter is finally concluded if—
-- src:14090 | (a) no meetings are to be summoned under section 3 of the Insolvency Act 1986 (c. 45) or Article 16 of the Insolvency (Northern Ireland) Order 1989,
-- src:14091 | (b) meetings summoned under that section or Article fail to approve the arrangement with no, or the same, modifications,
-- src:14092 | (c) an arrangement approved by meetings summoned under that section, or in consequence of a direction under section 6(4)(b) of that Act or Article 19(4)(b) of that Order, has been fully implemented, or
-- src:14093 | (d) the court makes an order under section 6(5) of that Act or Article 19(5) of that Order revoking approval given at previous meetings and, if the court gives any directions under section 6(6) of that Act or Article 19(6) of that Order, the company has done whatever it is required to do under those directions.
@ref s 1005(3) Circumstances in which application not to be made: other proceedings not concluded (src:14089-14093)
GIVEN `no meetings are to be summoned under section 3 of the Insolvency Act 1986 or Article 16 of the Insolvency (Northern Ireland) Order 1989` IS A BOOLEAN
      `meetings summoned under that section or Article fail to approve the arrangement with no, or the same, modifications` IS A BOOLEAN
      `an arrangement approved by meetings summoned under that section, or in consequence of a direction under section 6(4)(b) of that Act or Article 19(4)(b) of that Order, has been fully implemented` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court makes an order under section 6(5) of that Act or Article 19(5) of that Order revoking approval given at previous meetings` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company has done whatever it is required to do under any directions given by the court under section 6(6) of that Act or Article 19(6) of that Order` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1005(3) the matter of the voluntary arrangement is finally concluded` MEANS
    IF     `no meetings are to be summoned under section 3 of the Insolvency Act 1986 or Article 16 of the Insolvency (Northern Ireland) Order 1989`
       OR  `meetings summoned under that section or Article fail to approve the arrangement with no, or the same, modifications`
       OR  `an arrangement approved by meetings summoned under that section, or in consequence of a direction under section 6(4)(b) of that Act or Article 19(4)(b) of that Order, has been fully implemented`
       OR  (    `the court makes an order under section 6(5) of that Act or Article 19(5) of that Order revoking approval given at previous meetings`
            AND `the company has done whatever it is required to do under any directions given by the court under section 6(6) of that Act or Article 19(6) of that Order`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the matter is finally concluded if—"

-- (1) An application under section 1003 on behalf of a company must not be made at a time when (a) a Part 26 or 26A
-- application is pending, (b) a voluntary arrangement is pending, (c) the company is in administration, (d) the
-- interim moratorium applies, (e) the company is being wound up or a winding-up petition is pending, (f) there is a
-- receiver or manager of the company's property, or (g) a judicial factor administers the company's estate.
-- src:14077 | (1) An application under section 1003 (application for voluntary striking off) on behalf of a company must not be made at a time when—
-- src:14078 | (a) an application to the court under Part 26 or 26A has been made on behalf of the company for the sanctioning of a compromise or arrangement and the matter has not been finally concluded;
-- src:14079 | (b) a voluntary arrangement in relation to the company has been proposed under Part 1 of the Insolvency Act 1986 (c. 45) or Part 2 of the Insolvency (Northern Ireland) Order 1989 (S.I. 1989/2405 (N.I. 19)) and the matter has not been finally concluded;
-- src:14080 | (c) the company is in administration under Part 2 of that Act or Part 3 of that Order;
-- src:14081 | (d) paragraph 44 of Schedule B1 to that Act or paragraph 45 of Schedule B1 to that Order applies (interim moratorium on proceedings where application to the court for an administration order has been made or notice of intention to appoint administrator has been filed);
-- src:14082 | (e) the company is being wound up under Part 4 of that Act or Part 5 of that Order, whether voluntarily or by the court, or a petition under that Part for winding up of the company by the court has been presented and not finally dealt with or withdrawn;
-- src:14083 | (f) there is a receiver or manager of the company's property;
-- src:14084 | (g) the company's estate is being administered by a judicial factor.
@ref s 1005(1) Circumstances in which application not to be made: other proceedings not concluded (src:14077-14084)
GIVEN `an application to the court under Part 26 or 26A has been made on behalf of the company for the sanctioning of a compromise or arrangement` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 1005(2) the matter of the application to the court under Part 26 or 26A is finally concluded` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `a voluntary arrangement in relation to the company has been proposed under Part 1 of the Insolvency Act 1986 or Part 2 of the Insolvency (Northern Ireland) Order 1989` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 1005(3) the matter of the voluntary arrangement is finally concluded` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the company is in administration under Part 2 of that Act or Part 3 of that Order` IS A BOOLEAN
      `paragraph 44 of Schedule B1 to that Act or paragraph 45 of Schedule B1 to that Order applies (interim moratorium on proceedings)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company is being wound up under Part 4 of that Act or Part 5 of that Order, whether voluntarily or by the court` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a petition under that Part for winding up of the company by the court has been presented and not finally dealt with or withdrawn` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there is a receiver or manager of the company's property` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company's estate is being administered by a judicial factor` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1005(1) the application must not be made` MEANS
    IF     (    `an application to the court under Part 26 or 26A has been made on behalf of the company for the sanctioning of a compromise or arrangement`
            AND `s 1005(2) the matter of the application to the court under Part 26 or 26A is finally concluded` EQUALS JUST FALSE)
       OR  (    `a voluntary arrangement in relation to the company has been proposed under Part 1 of the Insolvency Act 1986 or Part 2 of the Insolvency (Northern Ireland) Order 1989`
            AND `s 1005(3) the matter of the voluntary arrangement is finally concluded` EQUALS JUST FALSE)
       OR  `the company is in administration under Part 2 of that Act or Part 3 of that Order`
       OR  `paragraph 44 of Schedule B1 to that Act or paragraph 45 of Schedule B1 to that Order applies (interim moratorium on proceedings)`
       OR  `the company is being wound up under Part 4 of that Act or Part 5 of that Order, whether voluntarily or by the court`
       OR  `a petition under that Part for winding up of the company by the court has been presented and not finally dealt with or withdrawn`
       OR  `there is a receiver or manager of the company's property`
       OR  `the company's estate is being administered by a judicial factor`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE IF     (    `an application to the court under Part 26 or 26A has been made on behalf of the company for the sanctioning of a compromise or arrangement`
                 AND `s 1005(2) the matter of the application to the court under Part 26 or 26A is finally concluded` EQUALS NOTHING)
            OR  (    `a voluntary arrangement in relation to the company has been proposed under Part 1 of the Insolvency Act 1986 or Part 2 of the Insolvency (Northern Ireland) Order 1989`
                 AND `s 1005(3) the matter of the voluntary arrangement is finally concluded` EQUALS NOTHING)
         THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether a pending matter is finally concluded is not known, and no other limb is shown
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must not be made at a time when— (a) an application to the court under Part 26 or 26A has been made ... and the matter has not been finally concluded" and the other six limbs ("when" counts as "where", ruled 2026-11-05)

-- (1) as a regulative rule: a director SHANT make the application (no time limit: the text gives none).
DECLARE `s 1005 act of the director` IS ONE OF
    `s 1005 make an application under section 1003 on behalf of the company`

