-- ---- s 1006: Copy of application to be given to members, employees, etc ----------------------------------------

-- (1) A person who makes an application under section 1003 on behalf of a company must secure that, within seven days
-- from the day on which the application is made, a copy is given to every person who at any time on that day is
-- (a) a member, (b) an employee, (c) a creditor, (d) a director, (e) a manager or trustee of a pension fund
-- established for the benefit of employees, or (f) a person of a description specified by regulations.
-- src:14100 | (1) A person who makes an application under section 1003 (application for voluntary striking off) on behalf of a company must secure that, within seven days from the day on which the application is made, a copy of it is given to every person who at any time on that day is—
-- src:14101 | (a) a member of the company,
-- src:14102 | (b) an employee of the company,
-- src:14103 | (c) a creditor of the company,
-- src:14104 | (d) a director of the company,
-- src:14105 | (e) a manager or trustee of any pension fund established for the benefit of employees of the company, or
-- src:14106 | (f) a person of a description specified for the purposes of this paragraph by regulations made by the Secretary of State.
-- src:14107 | Regulations under paragraph (f) are subject to negative resolution procedure.
@ref s 1006(1) Copy of application to be given to members, employees, etc (src:14100-14107)
GIVEN `the person is a member of the company on the day the application is made` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is an employee of the company on that day` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 1011 the person is a creditor of the company for the purposes of Chapter 1 of Part 31` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person is a director of the company on that day` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a manager or trustee of a pension fund established for the benefit of employees of the company on that day` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is of a description specified for the purposes of section 1006(1)(f) by regulations made by the Secretary of State` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1006(1) the person is one of those to whom a copy of the application must be given` MEANS
    IF     `the person is a member of the company on the day the application is made`
       OR  `the person is an employee of the company on that day`
       OR  `s 1011 the person is a creditor of the company for the purposes of Chapter 1 of Part 31` EQUALS JUST TRUE
       OR  `the person is a director of the company on that day`
       OR  `the person is a manager or trustee of a pension fund established for the benefit of employees of the company on that day`
       OR  `the person is of a description specified for the purposes of section 1006(1)(f) by regulations made by the Secretary of State`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "every person who at any time on that day is— (a) a member ... (f) a person of a description specified"; no "only" closes the list (a creditor seam that is open also lands here)

-- (2) Subsection (1) does not require a copy of the application to be given to a director who is a party to it.
-- src:14108 | (2) Subsection (1) does not require a copy of the application to be given to a director who is a party to the application.
@ref s 1006(2) Copy of application to be given to members, employees, etc (src:14108)
GIVEN `the person is a director of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the director is a party to the application` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1006(2) subsection (1) requires a copy of the application to be given to the director` MEANS
    IF `the person is a director of the company` AND `the director is a party to the application`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subsection (1) does not require a copy of the application to be given to a director who is a party to the application"
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): subsection (2) says only that a director who is a party is excused

-- (1) The last day for giving the copy: seven days from the day on which the application is made.
-- src:14100 | (1) A person who makes an application under section 1003 (application for voluntary striking off) on behalf of a company must secure that, within seven days from the day on which the application is made, a copy of it is given to every person who at any time on that day is—
-- src:14101 | (a) a member of the company,
-- src:14102 | (b) an employee of the company,
-- src:14103 | (c) a creditor of the company,
-- src:14104 | (d) a director of the company,
-- src:14105 | (e) a manager or trustee of any pension fund established for the benefit of employees of the company, or
-- src:14106 | (f) a person of a description specified for the purposes of this paragraph by regulations made by the Secretary of State.
-- src:14107 | Regulations under paragraph (f) are subject to negative resolution procedure.
@ref s 1006(1) Copy of application to be given to members, employees, etc (src:14100-14107)
GIVEN `the day on which the application is made` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 1006(1) the last day for giving the copy of the application` MEANS
    `the day on which the application is made` PLUS 7

@ref s 1006(1) Copy of application to be given to members, employees, etc (src:14100-14107)
GIVEN `the day on which the application is made` IS A DATE
      `the day on which the copy was given to the person` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1006(1) the copy of the application was given within the time allowed` MEANS
    IF `the day on which the copy was given to the person` AT MOST `s 1006(1) the last day for giving the copy of the application` `the day on which the application is made`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "within seven days from the day on which the application is made, a copy of it is given to every person" (the copy was given later)

-- (3) The duty ceases to apply if the application is withdrawn before the end of the period for giving the copy.
-- src:14109 | (3) The duty imposed by this section ceases to apply if the application is withdrawn before the end of the period for giving the copy application.
@ref s 1006(3) Copy of application to be given to members, employees, etc (src:14109)
GIVEN `the day on which the application is made` IS A DATE
      `the day on which the application was withdrawn, if it was` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1006(3) the duty imposed by section 1006 has ceased to apply` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the day on which the application was withdrawn, if it was`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "ceases to apply if the application is withdrawn before the end of the period for giving the copy application" (not withdrawn)
    WHEN JUST withdrawn THEN
        IF withdrawn AT MOST `s 1006(1) the last day for giving the copy of the application` `the day on which the application is made`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "ceases to apply if the application is withdrawn before the end of the period for giving the copy application" (withdrawn after the period ended)

-- (1) with (2): the duty owed to the person.
-- src:14100 | (1) A person who makes an application under section 1003 (application for voluntary striking off) on behalf of a company must secure that, within seven days from the day on which the application is made, a copy of it is given to every person who at any time on that day is—
-- src:14101 | (a) a member of the company,
-- src:14102 | (b) an employee of the company,
-- src:14103 | (c) a creditor of the company,
-- src:14104 | (d) a director of the company,
-- src:14105 | (e) a manager or trustee of any pension fund established for the benefit of employees of the company, or
-- src:14106 | (f) a person of a description specified for the purposes of this paragraph by regulations made by the Secretary of State.
-- src:14107 | Regulations under paragraph (f) are subject to negative resolution procedure.
-- src:14108 | (2) Subsection (1) does not require a copy of the application to be given to a director who is a party to the application.
@ref s 1006(1) Copy of application to be given to members, employees, etc (src:14100-14108)
GIVEN `s 1006(1) the person is one of those to whom a copy of the application must be given` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 1006(2) subsection (1) requires a copy of the application to be given to the director` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 1006(3) the duty imposed by section 1006 has ceased to apply` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1006(1) the applicant must secure that a copy of the application is given to the person` MEANS
    IF `s 1006(3) the duty imposed by section 1006 has ceased to apply` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The duty imposed by this section ceases to apply if the application is withdrawn before the end of the period"
    ELSE IF `s 1006(2) subsection (1) requires a copy of the application to be given to the director` EQUALS JUST FALSE
         THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subsection (1) does not require a copy of the application to be given to a director who is a party to the application"
         ELSE `s 1006(1) the person is one of those to whom a copy of the application must be given`

-- (1) as a regulative rule: the director who makes the application MUST secure that a copy is given WITHIN 7 days.
DECLARE `s 1006 act of the director` IS ONE OF
    `s 1006 secure that a copy of the application is given to the person`

-- src:14100 | (1) A person who makes an application under section 1003 (application for voluntary striking off) on behalf of a company must secure that, within seven days from the day on which the application is made, a copy of it is given to every person who at any time on that day is—
-- src:14101 | (a) a member of the company,
-- src:14102 | (b) an employee of the company,
-- src:14103 | (c) a creditor of the company,
-- src:14104 | (d) a director of the company,
-- src:14105 | (e) a manager or trustee of any pension fund established for the benefit of employees of the company, or
-- src:14106 | (f) a person of a description specified for the purposes of this paragraph by regulations made by the Secretary of State.
-- src:14107 | Regulations under paragraph (f) are subject to negative resolution procedure.
@ref s 1006(1) Copy of application to be given to members, employees, etc (src:14100-14107)
GIVEN `s 1006(1) the applicant must secure that a copy of the application is given to the person` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 1006 act of the director`
`s 1006(1) the director's duty to secure that a copy of the application is given` MEANS
    IF `s 1006(1) the applicant must secure that a copy of the application is given to the person` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN PARTY Director
         MUST `s 1006 secure that a copy of the application is given to the person`
         WITHIN 7
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST BREACH BY Director BECAUSE "a copy of the application was not given within seven days from the day on which the application was made"
    ELSE FULFILLED

-- (4) A person who fails to perform the duty imposed on him by this section commits an offence. If he does so with the
-- intention of concealing the making of the application from the person concerned, he commits an aggravated offence.
-- src:14110 | (4) A person who fails to perform the duty imposed on him by this section commits an offence.
-- src:14111 | If he does so with the intention of concealing the making of the application from the person concerned, he commits an aggravated offence.
@ref s 1006(4) Copy of application to be given to members, employees, etc (src:14110-14111)
GIVEN `s 1006(1) the applicant must secure that a copy of the application is given to the person` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the applicant failed to perform the duty` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1006(4) the person commits an offence by failing to perform the duty` MEANS
    IF `s 1006(1) the applicant must secure that a copy of the application is given to the person` EQUALS JUST TRUE AND `the applicant failed to perform the duty`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A person who fails to perform the duty imposed on him by this section commits an offence"; a person on whom no duty is imposed, or who performed it, is not mentioned (marginal reading (b))

@ref s 1006(4) Copy of application to be given to members, employees, etc (src:14110-14111)
GIVEN `s 1006(4) the person commits an offence by failing to perform the duty` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the failure was with the intention of concealing the making of the application from the person concerned` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1006(4) the person commits an aggravated offence by failing to perform the duty with the intention of concealing the application` MEANS
    IF `s 1006(4) the person commits an offence by failing to perform the duty` EQUALS JUST TRUE AND `the failure was with the intention of concealing the making of the application from the person concerned`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If he does so with the intention of concealing the making of the application from the person concerned, he commits an aggravated offence"

-- (5) In proceedings for an offence under this section it is a defence for the accused to prove that he took all
-- reasonable steps to perform the duty.
-- src:14112 | (5) In proceedings for an offence under this section it is a defence for the accused to prove that he took all reasonable steps to perform the duty.
@ref s 1006(5) Copy of application to be given to members, employees, etc (src:14112)
GIVEN `the accused proves that he took all reasonable steps to perform the duty` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1006(5) section 1006 gives the accused a defence on these facts` MEANS
    IF `the accused proves that he took all reasonable steps to perform the duty`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "it is a defence for the accused to prove that he took all reasonable steps to perform the duty" (this section gives no defence on these facts, ruled 2026-11-05 (b))

-- (6) A person guilty of an offence (other than an aggravated offence): (a) on conviction on indictment, a fine;
-- (b) on summary conviction, a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum.
-- src:14113 | (6) A person guilty of an offence under this section (other than an aggravated offence) is liable—
-- src:14114 | (a) on conviction on indictment, to a fine;
-- src:14115 | (b) on summary conviction, to a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum.
@ref s 1006(6) Copy of application to be given to members, employees, etc (src:14113-14115)
GIVETH A LIST OF Penalty
`s 1006(6) the penalty for a person guilty of an offence under section 1006` MEANS
    LIST
        (Penalty OF `on conviction on indictment`, NOTHING, JUST `a fine without a stated limit`, NOTHING, FALSE),
        (Penalty OF `on summary conviction`, NOTHING, JUST (`a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum` 1), NOTHING, FALSE)


-- (7) A person guilty of an aggravated offence: on indictment, imprisonment up to seven years or a fine (or both); on
-- summary conviction, in England and Wales up to twelve months or a fine up to the statutory maximum (or both), in
-- Scotland or Northern Ireland up to six months or a fine up to the statutory maximum (or both).
-- src:14116 | (7) A person guilty of an aggravated offence under this section is liable—
-- src:14117 | (a) on conviction on indictment, to imprisonment for a term not exceeding seven years or a fine (or both);
-- src:14118 | (b) on summary conviction—
-- src:14119 | (i) in England and Wales, to imprisonment for a term not exceeding twelve months or to a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum (or both);
-- src:14120 | (ii) in Scotland or Northern Ireland, to imprisonment for a term not exceeding six months, or to a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum (or both).
@ref s 1006(7) Copy of application to be given to members, employees, etc (src:14116-14120)
GIVETH A LIST OF Penalty
`s 1006(7) the penalty for a person guilty of an aggravated offence under section 1006` MEANS
    LIST
        (Penalty OF `on conviction on indictment`, JUST (Period OF 7, Years), JUST `a fine without a stated limit`, NOTHING, TRUE),
        (Penalty OF `on summary conviction in England and Wales`, JUST (Period OF 12, Months), JUST (`a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum` 1), NOTHING, TRUE),
        (Penalty OF `on summary conviction in Scotland`, JUST (Period OF 6, Months), JUST (`a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum` 1), NOTHING, TRUE),
        (Penalty OF `on summary conviction in Northern Ireland`, JUST (Period OF 6, Months), JUST (`a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum` 1), NOTHING, TRUE)


-- ---- s 1007: Copy of application to be given to new members, employees, etc -------------------------------

-- (1) The section applies in relation to any time after the day on which a company makes an application under
-- section 1003 and before the day on which the application is finally dealt with or withdrawn.
-- src:14122 | (1) This section applies in relation to any time after the day on which a company makes an application under section 1003 (application for voluntary striking off) and before the day on which the application is finally dealt with or withdrawn.
@ref s 1007(1) Copy of application to be given to new members, employees, etc (src:14122)
GIVEN `the day on which the company makes the application` IS A DATE
      `the day on which the application is finally dealt with or withdrawn, if it has been` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the day asked about` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1007(1) section 1007 applies to the day asked about` MEANS
    IF `the day asked about` GREATER THAN `the day on which the company makes the application`
    THEN CONSIDER `the day on which the application is finally dealt with or withdrawn, if it has been`
         WHEN NOTHING THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN JUST ended THEN
             IF `the day asked about` LESS THAN ended
             THEN JUST TRUE
             ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "any time after the day on which a company makes an application ... and before the day on which the application is finally dealt with or withdrawn" (the day is not before the day the application was dealt with or withdrawn)
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "any time after the day on which a company makes an application" (the day is not after the day of the application)

-- (2) A person who is a director of the company at the end of a day on which a person (other than himself) becomes
-- (a) a member, (b) an employee, (c) a creditor, (d) a director, (e) a manager or trustee of a pension fund, or
-- (f) a person of a description specified by regulations, must secure that a copy of the application is given to that
-- person within seven days from that day.
-- src:14123 | (2) A person who is a director of the company at the end of a day on which a person (other than himself) becomes—
-- src:14124 | (a) a member of the company,
-- src:14125 | (b) an employee of the company,
-- src:14126 | (c) a creditor of the company,
-- src:14127 | (d) a director of the company,
-- src:14128 | (e) a manager or trustee of any pension fund established for the benefit of employees of the company, or
-- src:14129 | (f) a person of a description specified for the purposes of this paragraph by regulations made by the Secretary of State,
-- src:14130 | must secure that a copy of the application is given to that person within seven days from that day.
-- src:14131 | Regulations under paragraph (f) are subject to negative resolution procedure.
@ref s 1007(2) Copy of application to be given to new members, employees, etc (src:14123-14131)
GIVEN `the other person becomes a member of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the other person becomes an employee of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 1011 the person is a creditor of the company for the purposes of Chapter 1 of Part 31` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the other person becomes a director of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the other person becomes a manager or trustee of a pension fund established for the benefit of employees of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the other person becomes a person of a description specified for the purposes of section 1007(2)(f) by regulations made by the Secretary of State` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1007(2) the other person becomes one of those to whom a copy of the application must be given` MEANS
    IF     `the other person becomes a member of the company`
       OR  `the other person becomes an employee of the company`
       OR  `s 1011 the person is a creditor of the company for the purposes of Chapter 1 of Part 31` EQUALS JUST TRUE
       OR  `the other person becomes a director of the company`
       OR  `the other person becomes a manager or trustee of a pension fund established for the benefit of employees of the company`
       OR  `the other person becomes a person of a description specified for the purposes of section 1007(2)(f) by regulations made by the Secretary of State`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "a person (other than himself) becomes— (a) a member of the company ... (f) a person of a description specified"; no "only" closes the list

@ref s 1007(2) Copy of application to be given to new members, employees, etc (src:14123-14131)
GIVEN `s 1007(1) section 1007 applies to the day asked about` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person is a director of the company at the end of the day on which the other person becomes one of those listed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the other person is someone other than the director himself` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 1007(2) the other person becomes one of those to whom a copy of the application must be given` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1007(2) the director must secure that a copy of the application is given to the other person` MEANS
    IF `s 1007(1) section 1007 applies to the day asked about` EQUALS JUST FALSE
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This section applies in relation to any time after the day on which a company makes an application ... and before the day on which the application is finally dealt with or withdrawn"
    ELSE IF NOT (`the other person is someone other than the director himself`)
         THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a person (other than himself) becomes"
         ELSE IF     `s 1007(1) section 1007 applies to the day asked about` EQUALS JUST TRUE
                 AND `the person is a director of the company at the end of the day on which the other person becomes one of those listed`
                 AND `s 1007(2) the other person becomes one of those to whom a copy of the application must be given` EQUALS JUST TRUE
              THEN JUST TRUE
              ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A person who is a director of the company at the end of a day on which a person (other than himself) becomes"; a person who is not such a director, or an event not listed, is not mentioned

-- (2) The last day for giving the copy: seven days from the day on which the other person becomes one of those listed.
@ref s 1007(2) Copy of application to be given to new members, employees, etc (src:14123-14131)
GIVEN `the day on which the other person becomes one of those listed` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 1007(2) the last day for giving the copy of the application` MEANS
    `the day on which the other person becomes one of those listed` PLUS 7

@ref s 1007(2) Copy of application to be given to new members, employees, etc (src:14123-14131)
GIVEN `the day on which the other person becomes one of those listed` IS A DATE
      `the day on which the copy was given to the other person` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1007(2) the copy of the application was given within the time allowed` MEANS
    IF `the day on which the copy was given to the other person` AT MOST `s 1007(2) the last day for giving the copy of the application` `the day on which the other person becomes one of those listed`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must secure that a copy of the application is given to that person within seven days from that day" (the copy was given later)

-- (3) The duty ceases to apply if the application is finally dealt with or withdrawn before the end of the period for
-- giving the copy.
-- src:14132 | (3) The duty imposed by this section ceases to apply if the application is finally dealt with or withdrawn before the end of the period for giving the copy application.
@ref s 1007(3) Copy of application to be given to new members, employees, etc (src:14132)
GIVEN `the day on which the other person becomes one of those listed` IS A DATE
      `the day on which the application was finally dealt with or withdrawn, if it was` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1007(3) the duty imposed by section 1007 has ceased to apply` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the day on which the application was finally dealt with or withdrawn, if it was`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "ceases to apply if the application is finally dealt with or withdrawn before the end of the period for giving the copy application" (not yet dealt with or withdrawn)
    WHEN JUST ended THEN
        IF ended AT MOST `s 1007(2) the last day for giving the copy of the application` `the day on which the other person becomes one of those listed`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "ceases to apply if the application is finally dealt with or withdrawn before the end of the period for giving the copy application" (dealt with or withdrawn after the period ended)

-- (2) as a regulative rule: the director MUST secure that a copy is given WITHIN 7 days.
DECLARE `s 1007 act of the director` IS ONE OF
    `s 1007 secure that a copy of the application is given to the other person`

-- src:14123 | (2) A person who is a director of the company at the end of a day on which a person (other than himself) becomes—
-- src:14124 | (a) a member of the company,
-- src:14125 | (b) an employee of the company,
-- src:14126 | (c) a creditor of the company,
-- src:14127 | (d) a director of the company,
-- src:14128 | (e) a manager or trustee of any pension fund established for the benefit of employees of the company, or
-- src:14129 | (f) a person of a description specified for the purposes of this paragraph by regulations made by the Secretary of State,
-- src:14130 | must secure that a copy of the application is given to that person within seven days from that day.
-- src:14131 | Regulations under paragraph (f) are subject to negative resolution procedure.
@ref s 1007(2) Copy of application to be given to new members, employees, etc (src:14123-14131)
GIVEN `s 1007(2) the director must secure that a copy of the application is given to the other person` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 1007 act of the director`
`s 1007(2) the director's duty to secure that a copy of the application is given to the other person` MEANS
    IF `s 1007(2) the director must secure that a copy of the application is given to the other person` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN PARTY Director
         MUST `s 1007 secure that a copy of the application is given to the other person`
         WITHIN 7
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST BREACH BY Director BECAUSE "a copy of the application was not given to the other person within seven days from the day on which that person became one of those listed"
    ELSE FULFILLED

-- (4) A person who fails to perform the duty commits an offence; with the intention of concealing the making of the
-- application from the person concerned, an aggravated offence.
-- src:14133 | (4) A person who fails to perform the duty imposed on him by this section commits an offence.
-- src:14134 | If he does so with the intention of concealing the making of the application from the person concerned, he commits an aggravated offence.
@ref s 1007(4) Copy of application to be given to new members, employees, etc (src:14133-14134)
GIVEN `s 1007(2) the director must secure that a copy of the application is given to the other person` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the director failed to perform the duty` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1007(4) the person commits an offence by failing to perform the duty` MEANS
    IF `s 1007(2) the director must secure that a copy of the application is given to the other person` EQUALS JUST TRUE AND `the director failed to perform the duty`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A person who fails to perform the duty imposed on him by this section commits an offence"; a person on whom no duty is imposed, or who performed it, is not mentioned (marginal reading (b))

@ref s 1007(4) Copy of application to be given to new members, employees, etc (src:14133-14134)
GIVEN `s 1007(4) the person commits an offence by failing to perform the duty` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the failure was with the intention of concealing the making of the application from the person concerned` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1007(4) the person commits an aggravated offence by failing to perform the duty with the intention of concealing the application` MEANS
    IF `s 1007(4) the person commits an offence by failing to perform the duty` EQUALS JUST TRUE AND `the failure was with the intention of concealing the making of the application from the person concerned`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If he does so with the intention of concealing the making of the application from the person concerned, he commits an aggravated offence"

-- (5) In proceedings for an offence under this section it is a defence for the accused to prove (a) that at the time of
-- the failure he was not aware of the fact that the company had made an application under section 1003, or (b) that
-- he took all reasonable steps to perform the duty.
-- src:14135 | (5) In proceedings for an offence under this section it is a defence for the accused to prove—
-- src:14136 | (a) that at the time of the failure he was not aware of the fact that the company had made an application under section 1003, or
-- src:14137 | (b) that he took all reasonable steps to perform the duty.
@ref s 1007(5) Copy of application to be given to new members, employees, etc (src:14135-14137)
GIVEN `the accused proves that at the time of the failure he was not aware of the fact that the company had made an application under section 1003` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the accused proves that he took all reasonable steps to perform the duty` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1007(5) section 1007 gives the accused a defence on these facts` MEANS
    IF     `the accused proves that at the time of the failure he was not aware of the fact that the company had made an application under section 1003`
       OR  `the accused proves that he took all reasonable steps to perform the duty`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "it is a defence for the accused to prove— (a) that at the time of the failure he was not aware of the fact that the company had made an application under section 1003, or (b) that he took all reasonable steps to perform the duty" (this section gives no defence on these facts, ruled 2026-11-05 (b))

