        (Penalty OF `on conviction on indictment`, JUST (Period OF 7, Years), JUST `a fine without a stated limit`, NOTHING, TRUE),
        (Penalty OF `on summary conviction in England and Wales`, JUST (Period OF 12, Months), JUST (`a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum` 1), NOTHING, TRUE),
        (Penalty OF `on summary conviction in Scotland`, JUST (Period OF 6, Months), JUST (`a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum` 1), NOTHING, TRUE),
        (Penalty OF `on summary conviction in Northern Ireland`, JUST (Period OF 6, Months), JUST (`a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum` 1), NOTHING, TRUE)


-- ---- s 1008: Copy of application: provisions as to service of documents -------------------------------------

-- (1) The provisions of section 1008 have effect for the purposes of sections 1006 and 1007.
-- src:14147 | (1) The following provisions have effect for the purposes of—
-- src:14148 | section 1006 (copy of application to be given to members, employees, etc), and
-- src:14149 | section 1007 (copy of application to be given to new members, employees, etc).
@ref s 1008(1) Copy of application: provisions as to service of documents (src:14147-14149)
DECLARE `s 1008(1) section whose service provisions are asked about` IS ONE OF
    `s 1008(1) section 1006 (copy of application to be given to members, employees, etc)`
    `s 1008(1) section 1007 (copy of application to be given to new members, employees, etc)`
    `s 1008(1) another section`

@ref s 1008(1) Copy of application: provisions as to service of documents (src:14147-14149)
GIVEN section IS A `s 1008(1) section whose service provisions are asked about`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1008(1) the provisions of section 1008 have effect for the purposes of the section` MEANS
    CONSIDER section
    WHEN `s 1008(1) section 1006 (copy of application to be given to members, employees, etc)` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 1008(1) section 1007 (copy of application to be given to new members, employees, etc)` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 1008(1) another section` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): section 1008 names sections 1006 and 1007 only, without "only"

-- (2) A document is treated as given to a person if it is (a) delivered to him, (b) left at his proper address, or
-- (c) sent by post to him at that address.
-- src:14150 | (2) A document is treated as given to a person if it is—
-- src:14151 | (a) delivered to him, or
-- src:14152 | (b) left at his proper address, or
-- src:14153 | (c) sent by post to him at that address.
@ref s 1008(2) Copy of application: provisions as to service of documents (src:14150-14153)
GIVEN `the document is delivered to the person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the document is left at the person's proper address` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the document is sent by post to the person at that address` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1008(2) the document is treated as given to the person` MEANS
    IF     `the document is delivered to the person`
       OR  `the document is left at the person's proper address`
       OR  `the document is sent by post to the person at that address`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A document is treated as given to a person if it is— (a) delivered to him, or (b) left at his proper address, or (c) sent by post to him at that address" (marginal reading (a): a deeming "if")

-- (3) For the purposes of subsection (2) and section 7 of the Interpretation Act 1978, the proper address of a person is
-- (a) for a firm incorporated or formed in the United Kingdom, its registered or principal office; (b) for a firm
-- incorporated or formed outside the United Kingdom, (i) if it has a place of business in the United Kingdom, its
-- principal office in the United Kingdom, or (ii) if not, its registered or principal office; (c) for an individual,
-- his last known address. "Firm" is any entity that is not an individual (section 1173(1)).
-- src:14154 | (3) For the purposes of subsection (2) and section 7 of the Interpretation Act 1978 (c. 30) (service of documents by post) as it applies in relation to that subsection, the proper address of a person is—
-- src:14155 | (a) in the case of a firm incorporated or formed in the United Kingdom, its registered or principal office;
-- src:14156 | (b) in the case of a firm incorporated or formed outside the United Kingdom—
-- src:14157 | (i) if it has a place of business in the United Kingdom, its principal office in the United Kingdom, or
-- src:14158 | (ii) if it does not have a place of business in the United Kingdom, its registered or principal office;
-- src:14159 | (c) in the case of an individual, his last known address.
@ref s 1008(3) Copy of application: provisions as to service of documents (src:14154-14159)
DECLARE `s 1008(3) proper address` IS ONE OF
    `s 1008(3)(a) the registered or principal office of the firm`
    `s 1008(3)(b)(i) the principal office of the firm in the United Kingdom`
    `s 1008(3)(b)(ii) the registered or principal office of the firm`
    `s 1008(3)(c) the individual's last known address`

@ref s 1008(3) Copy of application: provisions as to service of documents (src:14154-14159)
GIVEN `the person is an individual` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the firm is incorporated or formed in the United Kingdom` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the firm has a place of business in the United Kingdom` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `s 1008(3) proper address`
`s 1008(3) the proper address of the person` MEANS
    IF `the person is an individual`
    THEN `s 1008(3)(c) the individual's last known address`
    ELSE IF `the firm is incorporated or formed in the United Kingdom`
         THEN `s 1008(3)(a) the registered or principal office of the firm`
         ELSE IF `the firm has a place of business in the United Kingdom`
              THEN `s 1008(3)(b)(i) the principal office of the firm in the United Kingdom`
              ELSE `s 1008(3)(b)(ii) the registered or principal office of the firm`

-- (4) In the case of a creditor of the company a document is treated as given to him if it is left or sent by post to
-- him (a) at the place of business of his with which the company has had dealings by virtue of which he is a creditor,
-- or (b) if there is more than one such place of business, at each of them.
-- src:14160 | (4) In the case of a creditor of the company a document is treated as given to him if it is left or sent by post to him—
-- src:14161 | (a) at the place of business of his with which the company has had dealings by virtue of which he is a creditor of the company, or
-- src:14162 | (b) if there is more than one such place of business, at each of them.
@ref s 1008(4) Copy of application: provisions as to service of documents (src:14160-14162)
GIVEN `the person is a creditor of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the document is left or sent by post at the place of business of his with which the company has had dealings by virtue of which he is a creditor` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there is more than one such place of business` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the document is left or sent by post at each of them` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1008(4) the document is treated as given to the creditor` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the person is a creditor of the company`)
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "In the case of a creditor of the company"; other persons are for subsection (2)
    ELSE IF `there is more than one such place of business`
         THEN IF `the document is left or sent by post at each of them`
              THEN JUST TRUE
              ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if it is left or sent by post to him ... (b) if there is more than one such place of business, at each of them"
         ELSE IF `the document is left or sent by post at the place of business of his with which the company has had dealings by virtue of which he is a creditor`
              THEN JUST TRUE
              ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if it is left or sent by post to him— (a) at the place of business of his with which the company has had dealings by virtue of which he is a creditor"

-- ---- s 1009: Circumstances in which application to be withdrawn ---------------------------------------------

-- (1) The events, at any time on or after the day of the application and before it is finally dealt with or withdrawn.
-- src:14164 | (1) This section applies where, at any time on or after the day on which a company makes an application under section 1003 (application for voluntary striking off) and before the day on which the application is finally dealt with or withdrawn—
-- src:14165 | (a) the company—
-- src:14166 | (i) changes its name,
-- src:14167 | (ii) trades or otherwise carries on business,
-- src:14168 | (iii) makes a disposal for value of any property or rights other than those which it was necessary or expedient for it to hold for the purpose of making, or proceeding with, an application under that section, or
-- src:14169 | (iv) engages in any activity, except one to which subsection (4) applies;
-- src:14170 | (b) an application is made to the court under Part 26 or 26A on behalf of the company for the sanctioning of a compromise or arrangement;
-- src:14171 | (c) a voluntary arrangement in relation to the company is proposed under Part 1 of the Insolvency Act 1986 (c. 45) or Part 2 of the Insolvency (Northern Ireland) Order 1989 (S.I. 1989/2405 (N.I. 19));
-- src:14172 | (d) an application to the court for an administration order in respect of the company is made under paragraph 12 of Schedule B1 to that Act or paragraph 13 of Schedule B1 to that Order;
-- src:14173 | (e) an administrator is appointed in respect of the company under paragraph 14 or 22 of Schedule B1 to that Act or paragraph 15 or 23 of Schedule B1 to that Order, or a copy of notice of intention to appoint an administrator of the company under any of those provisions is filed with the court;
-- src:14174 | (f) there arise any of the circumstances in which, under section 84(1) of that Act or Article 70 of that Order, the company may be voluntarily wound up;
-- src:14175 | (g) a petition is presented for the winding up of the company by the court under Part 4 of that Act or Part 5 of that Order;
-- src:14176 | (h) a receiver or manager of the company's property is appointed; or
-- src:14177 | (i) a judicial factor is appointed to administer the company's estate.
@ref s 1009(1) Circumstances in which application to be withdrawn (src:14164-14177)
DECLARE `s 1009(1) event` IS ONE OF
    `s 1009(1)(a)(i) the company changes its name`
    `s 1009(1)(a)(ii) the company trades or otherwise carries on business`
    `s 1009(1)(a)(iii) the company makes a disposal for value of any property or rights other than those which it was necessary or expedient for it to hold for the purpose of making, or proceeding with, an application under section 1003`
    `s 1009(1)(a)(iv) the company engages in any activity, except one to which subsection (4) applies`
    `s 1009(1)(b) an application is made to the court under Part 26 or 26A on behalf of the company for the sanctioning of a compromise or arrangement`
    `s 1009(1)(c) a voluntary arrangement in relation to the company is proposed under Part 1 of the Insolvency Act 1986 or Part 2 of the Insolvency (Northern Ireland) Order 1989`
    `s 1009(1)(d) an application to the court for an administration order in respect of the company is made`
    `s 1009(1)(e) an administrator is appointed in respect of the company, or a copy of notice of intention to appoint an administrator is filed with the court`
    `s 1009(1)(f) there arise circumstances in which the company may be voluntarily wound up under section 84(1) of that Act or Article 70 of that Order`
    `s 1009(1)(g) a petition is presented for the winding up of the company by the court under Part 4 of that Act or Part 5 of that Order`
    `s 1009(1)(h) a receiver or manager of the company's property is appointed`
    `s 1009(1)(i) a judicial factor is appointed to administer the company's estate`

-- (3) For the purposes of subsection (1)(a) a company is not treated as trading or otherwise carrying on business by
-- virtue only of the fact that it makes a payment in respect of a liability incurred in the course of trading.
-- src:14179 | (3) For the purposes of subsection (1)(a), a company is not treated as trading or otherwise carrying on business by virtue only of the fact that it makes a payment in respect of a liability incurred in the course of trading or otherwise carrying on business.
@ref s 1009(3) Circumstances in which application to be withdrawn (src:14179)
GIVEN `the company traded or otherwise carried on business` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the only reason is that the company makes a payment in respect of a liability incurred in the course of trading or otherwise carrying on business` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1009(3) the company is treated as trading or otherwise carrying on business` MEANS
    IF `the only reason is that the company makes a payment in respect of a liability incurred in the course of trading or otherwise carrying on business`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a company is not treated as trading or otherwise carrying on business by virtue only of the fact that it makes a payment in respect of a liability incurred in the course of trading or otherwise carrying on business"
    ELSE IF `the company traded or otherwise carried on business`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection says when a company is not treated as trading, and says nothing about a company that did not trade

-- (4) The excepted activities referred to in subsection (1)(a)(iv) are (a) any activity necessary or expedient for the
-- purposes of (i) making, or proceeding with, an application under section 1003, (ii) concluding affairs of the
-- company that are outstanding because of what has been necessary or expedient for that, (iii) complying with any
-- statutory requirement; (b) any activity specified by the Secretary of State by order for the purposes of subsection (4).
-- src:14180 | (4) The excepted activities referred to in subsection (1)(a)(iv) are—
-- src:14181 | (a) any activity necessary or expedient for the purposes of—
-- src:14182 | (i) making, or proceeding with, an application under section 1003 (application for voluntary striking off),
-- src:14183 | (ii) concluding affairs of the company that are outstanding because of what has been necessary or expedient for the purpose of making, or proceeding with, such an application, or
-- src:14184 | (iii) complying with any statutory requirement;
-- src:14185 | (b) any activity specified by the Secretary of State by order for the purposes of this subsection.
-- src:14186 | An order under paragraph (b) is subject to negative resolution procedure.
@ref s 1009(4) Circumstances in which application to be withdrawn (src:14180-14186)
GIVEN `the activity was necessary or expedient for the purposes of making, or proceeding with, an application under section 1003` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the activity was necessary or expedient for the purposes of concluding affairs of the company that are outstanding because of what has been necessary or expedient for the purpose of making, or proceeding with, such an application` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the activity was necessary or expedient for the purposes of complying with any statutory requirement` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the activity is specified by the Secretary of State by order for the purposes of section 1009(4)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1009(4) the activity is an excepted activity` MEANS
    IF     `the activity was necessary or expedient for the purposes of making, or proceeding with, an application under section 1003`
       OR  `the activity was necessary or expedient for the purposes of concluding affairs of the company that are outstanding because of what has been necessary or expedient for the purpose of making, or proceeding with, such an application`
       OR  `the activity was necessary or expedient for the purposes of complying with any statutory requirement`
       OR  `the activity is specified by the Secretary of State by order for the purposes of section 1009(4)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The excepted activities referred to in subsection (1)(a)(iv) are—" (a definition handed to a list: no head holds, ruled 2026-11-05 (a))

-- (1)(a)(iii) A disposal for value of any property or rights other than those which it was necessary or expedient for
-- it to hold for the purpose of making, or proceeding with, an application under section 1003.
-- src:14168 | (iii) makes a disposal for value of any property or rights other than those which it was necessary or expedient for it to hold for the purpose of making, or proceeding with, an application under that section, or
@ref s 1009(1)(a)(iii) Circumstances in which application to be withdrawn (src:14168)
GIVEN `the company makes a disposal for value of property or rights` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the property or rights were ones which it was necessary or expedient for it to hold for the purpose of making, or proceeding with, an application under section 1003` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1009(1)(a)(iii) the disposal is one that requires the application to be withdrawn` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the company makes a disposal for value of property or rights`)
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "makes a disposal for value of any property or rights" (no disposal)
    ELSE IF `the property or rights were ones which it was necessary or expedient for it to hold for the purpose of making, or proceeding with, an application under section 1003`
         THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "other than those which it was necessary or expedient for it to hold for the purpose of making, or proceeding with, an application under that section" (an "other than" exclusion: fork F8)
         ELSE JUST TRUE

-- (1)(a)(iv) Engages in any activity, except one to which subsection (4) applies.
-- src:14169 | (iv) engages in any activity, except one to which subsection (4) applies;
@ref s 1009(1)(a)(iv) Circumstances in which application to be withdrawn (src:14169)
GIVEN `the company engages in an activity` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 1009(4) the activity is an excepted activity` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1009(1)(a)(iv) the activity is one that requires the application to be withdrawn` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the company engages in an activity`)
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "engages in any activity" (no activity)
    ELSE CONSIDER `s 1009(4) the activity is an excepted activity`
         WHEN JUST excepted THEN
             IF excepted
             THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "except one to which subsection (4) applies"
             ELSE JUST TRUE
         WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the activity is an excepted activity is not known

-- (1) At least one of the events has occurred at a time on or after the day on which the company makes the
-- application under section 1003 and before the day on which the application is finally dealt with or withdrawn.
-- src:14164 | (1) This section applies where, at any time on or after the day on which a company makes an application under section 1003 (application for voluntary striking off) and before the day on which the application is finally dealt with or withdrawn—
-- src:14165 | (a) the company—
-- src:14166 | (i) changes its name,
-- src:14167 | (ii) trades or otherwise carries on business,
-- src:14168 | (iii) makes a disposal for value of any property or rights other than those which it was necessary or expedient for it to hold for the purpose of making, or proceeding with, an application under that section, or
-- src:14169 | (iv) engages in any activity, except one to which subsection (4) applies;
-- src:14170 | (b) an application is made to the court under Part 26 or 26A on behalf of the company for the sanctioning of a compromise or arrangement;
-- src:14171 | (c) a voluntary arrangement in relation to the company is proposed under Part 1 of the Insolvency Act 1986 (c. 45) or Part 2 of the Insolvency (Northern Ireland) Order 1989 (S.I. 1989/2405 (N.I. 19));
-- src:14172 | (d) an application to the court for an administration order in respect of the company is made under paragraph 12 of Schedule B1 to that Act or paragraph 13 of Schedule B1 to that Order;
-- src:14173 | (e) an administrator is appointed in respect of the company under paragraph 14 or 22 of Schedule B1 to that Act or paragraph 15 or 23 of Schedule B1 to that Order, or a copy of notice of intention to appoint an administrator of the company under any of those provisions is filed with the court;
-- src:14174 | (f) there arise any of the circumstances in which, under section 84(1) of that Act or Article 70 of that Order, the company may be voluntarily wound up;
-- src:14175 | (g) a petition is presented for the winding up of the company by the court under Part 4 of that Act or Part 5 of that Order;
-- src:14176 | (h) a receiver or manager of the company's property is appointed; or
-- src:14177 | (i) a judicial factor is appointed to administer the company's estate.
@ref s 1009(1) Circumstances in which application to be withdrawn (src:14164-14177)
GIVEN `the events that have occurred on or after the day on which the company makes the application and before the day on which it is finally dealt with or withdrawn` IS A LIST OF `s 1009(1) event`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1009(1) at least one of the events has occurred` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the events that have occurred on or after the day on which the company makes the application and before the day on which it is finally dealt with or withdrawn`
    WHEN EMPTY THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This section applies where, at any time on or after the day on which a company makes an application ... (a) the company— ... (i) changes its name" and the other events (none has occurred)
    WHEN event FOLLOWED BY otherEvents THEN JUST TRUE

-- (2) A person who, at the end of a day on which any of the events occurs, is a director of the company must secure
-- that the company's application is withdrawn forthwith.
-- src:14178 | (2) A person who, at the end of a day on which any of the events mentioned in subsection (1) occurs, is a director of the company must secure that the company's application is withdrawn forthwith.
@ref s 1009(2) Circumstances in which application to be withdrawn (src:14178)
GIVEN `s 1009(1) at least one of the events has occurred` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person is a director of the company at the end of a day on which one of the events occurs` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1009(2) the director must secure that the company's application is withdrawn forthwith` MEANS
    IF `s 1009(1) at least one of the events has occurred` EQUALS JUST FALSE
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This section applies where, at any time on or after the day on which a company makes an application under section 1003"
    ELSE IF `s 1009(1) at least one of the events has occurred` EQUALS JUST TRUE AND `the person is a director of the company at the end of a day on which one of the events occurs`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A person who, at the end of a day on which any of the events mentioned in subsection (1) occurs, is a director of the company"; a person who is not such a director is not mentioned

-- (2) as a regulative rule. "Forthwith" is not a number of days, so there is no WITHIN: with no act, the duty stays
-- open (a residual obligation), and an act at any time fulfils it. The decision function above carries the same duty.
DECLARE `s 1009 act of the director` IS ONE OF
    `s 1009 secure that the company's application is withdrawn`

-- src:14178 | (2) A person who, at the end of a day on which any of the events mentioned in subsection (1) occurs, is a director of the company must secure that the company's application is withdrawn forthwith.
@ref s 1009(2) Circumstances in which application to be withdrawn (src:14178)
GIVEN `s 1009(2) the director must secure that the company's application is withdrawn forthwith` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 1009 act of the director`
`s 1009(2) the director's duty to secure that the company's application is withdrawn` MEANS
    IF `s 1009(2) the director must secure that the company's application is withdrawn forthwith` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN PARTY Director
         MUST `s 1009 secure that the company's application is withdrawn`
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST BREACH BY Director BECAUSE "the company's application was not withdrawn forthwith"
    ELSE FULFILLED

-- (5) A person who fails to perform the duty imposed on him by this section commits an offence.
-- src:14187 | (5) A person who fails to perform the duty imposed on him by this section commits an offence.
@ref s 1009(5) Circumstances in which application to be withdrawn (src:14187)
GIVEN `s 1009(2) the director must secure that the company's application is withdrawn forthwith` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the director failed to perform the duty` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1009(5) the person commits an offence by failing to perform the duty` MEANS
    IF `s 1009(2) the director must secure that the company's application is withdrawn forthwith` EQUALS JUST TRUE AND `the director failed to perform the duty`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A person who fails to perform the duty imposed on him by this section commits an offence"; a person on whom no duty is imposed, or who performed it, is not mentioned (marginal reading (b))

-- (6) In proceedings for an offence under this section it is a defence for the accused to prove (a) that at the time of
-- the failure he was not aware of the fact that the company had made an application under section 1003, or (b) that
-- he took all reasonable steps to perform the duty.
-- src:14188 | (6) In proceedings for an offence under this section it is a defence for the accused to prove—
-- src:14189 | (a) that at the time of the failure he was not aware of the fact that the company had made an application under section 1003, or
-- src:14190 | (b) that he took all reasonable steps to perform the duty.
@ref s 1009(6) Circumstances in which application to be withdrawn (src:14188-14190)
GIVEN `the accused proves that at the time of the failure he was not aware of the fact that the company had made an application under section 1003` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the accused proves that he took all reasonable steps to perform the duty` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1009(6) section 1009 gives the accused a defence on these facts` MEANS
    IF     `the accused proves that at the time of the failure he was not aware of the fact that the company had made an application under section 1003`
       OR  `the accused proves that he took all reasonable steps to perform the duty`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "it is a defence for the accused to prove— (a) that at the time of the failure he was not aware of the fact that the company had made an application under section 1003, or (b) that he took all reasonable steps to perform the duty" (this section gives no defence on these facts, ruled 2026-11-05 (b))

-- (7) (a) on conviction on indictment, a fine; (b) on summary conviction, a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum.
-- src:14191 | (7) A person guilty of an offence under this section is liable—
-- src:14192 | (a) on conviction on indictment, to a fine;
-- src:14193 | (b) on summary conviction, to a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum.
@ref s 1009(7) Circumstances in which application to be withdrawn (src:14191-14193)
GIVETH A LIST OF Penalty
`s 1009(7) the penalty for a person guilty of an offence under section 1009` MEANS
    LIST
        (Penalty OF `on conviction on indictment`, NOTHING, JUST `a fine without a stated limit`, NOTHING, FALSE),
        (Penalty OF `on summary conviction`, NOTHING, JUST (`a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum` 1), NOTHING, FALSE)


-- ---- s 1010: Withdrawal of application ----------------------------------------------------------------------

-- An application under section 1003 is withdrawn by notice to the registrar.
-- src:14195 | An application under section 1003 is withdrawn by notice to the registrar.
@ref s 1010 Withdrawal of application (src:14195)
GIVEN `notice of withdrawal of the application has been given to the registrar` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1010 the application under section 1003 is withdrawn` MEANS
    IF `notice of withdrawal of the application has been given to the registrar`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the text says that notice is how an application is withdrawn, and says nothing about a withdrawal by any other means

-- ---- s 1011: Meaning of "creditor" ------------------------

-- In this Chapter "creditor" includes a contingent or prospective creditor. The text says "includes", so a person
-- who is none of the three is not covered rather than excluded.
-- src:14197 | In this Chapter “creditor” includes a contingent or prospective creditor.
@ref s 1011 Meaning of "creditor" (src:14197)
GIVEN `the person is a creditor of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a contingent creditor of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a prospective creditor of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1011 the person is a creditor of the company for the purposes of Chapter 1 of Part 31` MEANS
    IF     `the person is a creditor of the company`
       OR  `the person is a contingent creditor of the company`
       OR  `the person is a prospective creditor of the company`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "“creditor” includes a contingent or prospective creditor"
